+## Rejected (with reason)
+- [FYI] §2.4 Scope membership and Cost — `log`/`last_change` cost model omits per-commit scope resolution (slug-named folders force a seat enumeration per scanned commit). Mechanism is real (src/store/layout.rs:43-61, `locate` → `all_seats`), but no requirement sets a latency or scale target; §2.4 caps the scan at 5000, reports early stop, and explicitly defers an index/cache ("Not justified before real history sizes show a need"). Ground seat's dissent (Should-fix) is addressed by the majority: the fix is internal to HistoryWalker/Scope and changes no contract. Reject 2–1.
+- [FYI] §2.4 "Last change in the roster"; §2.2 Cost — Roster `last_change` walks up to 5000 commits on every daemon-free call. §2.4 costs and caps the walk, §2.6 marks it `(last_change)`, output shows `older than scan`; §2.2 Cost omitting it is a documentation inconsistency, not a requirement violation. Reject 2–1 (ground: Nit).
+- [FYI] §2.3 stack "the commit that last changed it"; HistoryWalker "last commit that touched path P" — Last-touch lookups have no scan cap or cost entry. HistoryWalker owns the cap and the lookup in one module; staleness is digest-driven so the commit id is decoration; spec defers a cache. Ground seat verified libgit2 issue #3041 (no path-limited revwalk) but rated Nit. Reject 2–1.
+- [FYI] §2.3 record shape (no native session id) — Ownership rests only on `at` vs `occupant.since`. Majority: every failure direction degrades to `unknown`, and a prior record cannot read as current since its `at` precedes the new `since`. The ground seat's evidence (line 110 ordering) is the same defect as the Blocking finding above; a session-id binding is listed there as a fix shape. Reject 2–1; not escalated because the majority's evidence addresses the ordering explicitly.
+- [FYI] Key abstractions Roster "The daemon's new `roster.live` command calls the same builder" — No execution budget / spawn_blocking / 30 s timeout. Cache-thrash premise fails (HistoryWalker does not call `locate`); walk is capped at 5000; compose.rs already uses spawn_blocking; SeatSlots plumbing is implied by lines 193 and 479. Reject 3–0.
+- [FYI] §2.3 harness-native files (user-level list) — Omits managed policy `/etc/claude-code/CLAUDE.md`, `~/.claude/rules/`, `.claude/AGENTS.md`, auto-memory MEMORY.md. Product decision 3 bounds the listing to presence/size/mtime; §1.2 puts harness-native files outside graph's knowledge; spec never claims completeness. Cheap list extension at most. Reject 3–0 (external facts taken as given, not fetched).
+- [FYI] §2.2 With `--live`; Roster Relationships — Who resolves scope / which HEAD for `roster --live`. Spec line 479: the daemon calls "the same builder", which owns scope resolution, loaded reads and the walk; §2.1 head rule applies; the CLI/daemon split in the finding is not in the spec. Reject 3–0.
+- [FYI] §2.5 Cost "`--since` filters on `started`" — Long-running session excluded from `sessions --since`. The rule is stated explicitly and matches the sort key; B4 does not ask for an "active in window" query; the session is visible without the flag. Reject 2–1.
+- [FYI] §2.4 Scope membership "resolved to IDs against that commit's own tree" — Deletions/moves resolved only in the commit tree. Moves and archive relocations resolve via the new path; tombstones are modifications; only a whole-folder removal is uncovered, and the spec already marks purge history as a limit. Reject 2–1.
+- [FYI] §2.2 "Without `--live` it is daemon-free and reads committed HEAD" — No freshness/daemon-liveness signal. §2.2 names `--live` as the answer to "running right now"; the rejected-options table drops heartbeats deliberately; envelope carries `live:false` and `runtime.observed_at`. Reject 3–0.
+- [FYI] §2.3 Status `stale`; LoadedInstructions comparison rule — Rename reports stale as removed+added. Labels are in the delivered text (`## <label> — <path>`), so the agent did receive different text; `stale` is accurate. Reject 3–0.
+- [FYI] §2.3 Status `unknown`; LoadedInstructions Errors — `unknown` merges four conditions with no reason field. Spec: "`unknown` is a real state, not an error"; write errors are deliberately swallowed; no requirement asks for write-failure diagnosis. Reject 2–1 (ground: Nit, suggests optional `unknown_reason`).
+- [FYI] §2.4/§2.5 `--since <date|dur>` — No grammar, timezone, inclusivity, error code. Filter field for `sessions` is stated (`started`); `log` rows carry commit time; usage errors map to existing exit codes; implementation detail for a design doc. Reject 2–1.
+- [FYI] §2.4 Scope membership (`seat` includes transcripts; `teamspace` does not) — Seat log not a subset of teamspace log. No subset invariant is stated; transcript processing is `bookkeeping` and hidden by default; divergence appears only under `--all`. Reject 3–0.
+- [FYI] §2.4 scopes; "Last change in the roster" — Seat scope omits template/teamspace/global edits that change the seat's stack. `log` is the "changes to" view by design; stack drift is covered by the `instructions` status column and `stale_parts` with commits (line 241). Reject 3–0.
+- [FYI] absent (§2.1 Principles; View output) — No SIGPIPE/BrokenPipe handling for new pipe-oriented commands. Pre-existing, repo-wide property of every existing reader (`list`, `show`); belongs in a CLI-wide `main` fix, not this design. Reject 3–0.
+- [FYI] §2.4 Journal side "The filter is on requester" — `ops --teamspace` misses ops whose requester teamspace was `None` or whose seat moved. §2.4 and §1 define the filter on the stored requester; retire.rs:6 and cycle_guard.rs:15-16 state no kind moves a seat between teamspaces today. Reject 3–0.
