+## Unverified nits (spot-checked)
+- [FYI] §2.3 "Who writes it … after it prints"; Honest limits — Record written after printing assumes hook output reached the model (timeouts, >10k-char replacement, compact-matcher bugs). Spot REJECT: "injected, not retained" limit already covers this; cited harness bugs not web-verified.
+- [FYI] §2.3 harness-native files; §4 decision 3 — "present" says nothing about loaded (`claudeMdExcludes`, on-demand subdirectory loading). Spot REJECT: presence-only is the user-bounded scope; at most a one-line "presence is not loading" note.
+- [FYI] §2.5 Limit (tombstone footer) — Footer cannot count purges that delete the record outright (src/threads/assignment.rs `purge_tombstone` `(None, None) => None`); tombstones carry no marker. Spot REJECT: spec already says purge may remove the record entirely and defers history recovery.
+- [FYI] Key abstractions Scope "one parser and one resolver at HEAD" — `log <scope>` cannot target a purged object or a former name. Spot REJECT: only clones are purged and `log` rejects clone scope; retired seats/teamspaces resolve from `archive/`; ids are accepted.
+- [FYI] §2.3 `instructions stack <seat> [--clone <c>]`; §2.2 "one render per active seat" — Behaviour for dormant/retired seats, seats with no clones, and `--clone` semantics undefined. Spot REJECT: §2.2 sample shows dormant seats as bare lines and retired clones as `unknown`; `stack` is a pure HEAD read for any seat; `--clone` is the obvious filter with existing Scope errors.
+- [FYI] §2.1 "The JSON is the contract"; module Errors lines — Exit codes only partly specified (empty result, scan cap, no-instance, bad `--since`/`--limit`). Spot REJECT: codes inherited by reference from `instructions show`/`seat --instructions`; cap hit is "a reported outcome, not an error" (line 467).
+- [FYI] §2.3 "in the seat's cwd (the `src/model/launch.rs` rule)" — Harness files located from the configured cwd, not the session's recorded `NativeSession.cwd`. Spot REJECT: graph launches the agent in that cwd; the "bound after creation" case is hypothetical.
+- [FYI] LoadedInstructions "last writer wins through rename" — Concurrent hook and `seat.resolve` writers can land out of order. Spot REJECT: needs two renders at different HEADs within milliseconds; worst case is one false label that self-heals on the next injection.
